<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN NOVEMBER TRACTOR SALES UP 58 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN NOVEMBER TRACTOR SALES UP 58 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Demand remained strong for tractors among South African farmers in November with sales reaching 586 units, up 58 percent on the same month last year, the South African Agricultural Machinery Association said.</p>
<p>On a year-to-date basis sales were 42.4 percent up on last year at 5,648.</p>
<p>Agricultural machinery sales have been boosted by a bumper maize crop and pre-emptive buying ahead of expected price rises due to the fall in the rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
